ite_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.7 stable.\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Vulkan renderer (Forward+) - RTX 5090.\n\n### Issue description\n\nHi! I found this in Godot 4.7 stable, but from what I can tell, the code for this has not been fixed in 4.7.1. It is not reproducible in the editor, or when exporting in debug mode, *only* in **release** mode.\n\nWhen using blas_create() in the Godot editor, everything seems to work fine until you export a release build. I found myself getting the error `The index buffer contains an index that is outside the specified vertex range.`. Looks like it comes from this code here:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/eda2a482e9ce82e4056cfffae0ea98c1954605a1/servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp#L4006-L4034\n\nNote that without DEBUG_ENABLED, the index buffer's max index is always `0xFFFFFFFF`. In other words, `max_index` is only computed when DEBUG_ENABLED. Whenever you add any real geometry, this will fail in release mode.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a BLAS with some geometry. Export in debug mode and in release mode. Note that release mode crashes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nHere you are:\n\nhttps://github.com/ejektaflex/godot-blas-fail-mrp","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"htt